From fd62ae38da32fd28d8f2821dfcb5ecee4238e9e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: machuanhu <1748771273@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 18:31:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(distributed): integrate unified_comm adapter into
 GroupCoordinator

Wire vllm.distributed.unified_comm.UnifiedCommAdapter into the
GroupCoordinator collective hot paths. The integration is strictly
opt-in via the UNIFIED_COMM_ENABLED=1 environment variable; when the
flag is unset, the default device_communicator code path is unchanged.

Changes in vllm/distributed/parallel_state.py:
- add class-level defaults (_unified_adapter / _unified_adapter_built)
  on GroupCoordinator so subclasses that override __init__ without
  calling super() (e.g. vllm-ascend-hust GroupCoordinatorPatch) still
  get safe fallback values
- add _get_unified_adapter() that lazily builds the adapter on first
  use, normalizes self.device when subclasses store it as an int from
  torch.npu.current_device(), and idempotently calls
  initialize_unified_comm() to populate the backend registry
- route _all_reduce_out_place / _all_gather_out_place /
  _reduce_scatter_out_place / broadcast through the adapter, falling
  back to the original device_communicator path when the adapter is
  None or returns None
- release the adapter from destroy() (the underlying ProcessGroup is
  reused, not owned, so torch.distributed cleanup is unaffected)

Tests in tests/distributed/test_unified_comm.py:
- single-process: feature flag plumbing (default off, multiple
  truthy/falsy spellings) and try_create() returning None when
  disabled
- multi-process (skipped when fewer than 2 accelerators): 2-rank
  smoke tests for all_reduce / all_gather / broadcast that compare
  numerical output against the values produced by the underlying
  torch.distributed PG

End-to-end validation on Ascend 910B2 x 2 with Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
TP=2 (random-online, 200 prompts, rate=1.0): 233.0 tok/s output
throughput, mean TPOT 77 ms, 0 / 200 failures. The same workload
without UNIFIED_COMM_ENABLED takes the unmodified code path; the new
hooks add a single class-attribute check on the cold path.

Signed-off-by: machuanhu <1748771273@qq.com>
